From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:40:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: Report the memory of the media cache

No memory reporter measured the media cache, so about:memory showed
neither the media that it keeps in memory nor what it keeps in its
temporary file.

Register a reporter for the cache of each process, next to the system
reporter: in the main process, where the cache lives in single-process
mode, and in every content process. Like the system reporter, it runs
on its own thread, since every script thread of the process shares the
cache, and it reports nothing until the cache is used. Under
`explicit/media-cache` it reports the heap memory of the resources that
are kept in memory, of the write buffers of the other resources, and of
the memory fallback when the temporary file cannot be used;
`media-cache-file` reports the data in the temporary file, which is in
the page cache rather than in the memory of the process.

`MediaCache::measure_memory` replaces the unused `MallocSizeOf`
implementation, and `MediaCache::existing` returns the cache of the
process without creating it.

Fork note: meant for upstream. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: unit tests of the measurement of each kind of data, of the
memory fallback, and of `MediaCache::existing`.

Validation: headless servoshell (`checked-release`) on Linux playing a 14.3 MB MP4 and a 96.9 KB WebM, then `navigator.servo.reportMemory()` with `expose_servointernals_globally`: in single-process mode the main process reports media-cache/resources-in-memory as 98304 bytes and media-cache-file as 14261838 bytes, the whole MP4; with `-M` the content process reports the same, and the main process nothing. `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release`, the same with `--ohos`, `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` (1153 tests) and `--doc` pass.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implemented and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
